────────────────────────────────────────
PRISMA & PERFORMANCE
────────────────────────────────────────

1) Prisma query discipline
- Prefer select over broad include.
- Avoid loading unnecessary relations.
- Avoid N+1 queries; use batched queries.
- Use consistent ordering for pagination.

2) Transactions
- Keep transactions short.
- Do NOT run heavy loops inside transactions.
- For "increment usage counters", use atomic updates.

3) Index-aware queries
- When creating new endpoints, ensure filtering uses indexed columns:
  - tenantId, createdAt, status, type, foreign keys

4) Multi-tenant integrity
- Every Prisma query touching tenant data must enforce tenant isolation.
- Cross-tenant queries require explicit platform authorization.

5) Migrations discipline
- Local dev: prisma migrate dev
- Production/CI (Vercel): prisma migrate deploy
- Do not introduce db push as a deployment mechanism.

6) Caching (efficiency)
- Cache plan/limits per request when safe (e.g. resolveTenantPlan for same tenantId).
- Do not cache tenant-scoped list/detail responses without explicit invalidation and tenant isolation.
- See docs/epics/00-EPIC-QUALITY-AND-PRACTICES.md §4 (Caching) for full guidance.
